<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0100018> rdfs:label "Nuclear cataract"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A nuclear cataract is an opacity or clouding that develops in the lens nucleus. That is, a nuclear cataract is one that is located in the center of the lens. The nucleus tends to darken changing from clear to yellow and sometimes brown." ;
