<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0030374> rdfs:label "Decreased proportion of memory B cells" ;
    dcterms:description "A reduction in the normal proportion of memory B cells (CD19+/CD27+) in circulation relative to the total number of B cells. Memory B cells develop from naive B cells. Upon antigen rechallenge, memory B cells rapidly expand and differentiate into plasma cells under the cognate control of memory Th cells (Phase IV)." ;
    ns1:category ns1:PhenotypicFeature ;
    ns1:xref "UMLS:C4072913" .

<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0030388> rdfs:label "Decreased class-switched memory B cell proportion"@en ;
    dcterms:description "A reduction in the normal proportion of class-switched memory B cells (CD19+/CD27+/IgM+/IgD+) relative to the total number of B cells. Marginal zone B cells undergo limited somatic hypermutation and produce high-affinity IgM and some IgG, whereas class-switched memory B cells synthetize IgG, IgM, and IgA." ;
    ns1:category ns1:PhenotypicFeature ;
    ns1:exact_synonym "Decreased proportion of CD19+CD27+IgD- cells",
        "Decreased proportion of class-switched memory B cells" ;
    ns1:synonym "Decreased proportion of CD19+CD27+IgD- cells",
        "Decreased proportion of class-switched memory B cells" ;
    ns1:xref "UMLS:C4072925" .

